    "Owned reply-only DeepSeek Flash samples used no tools or file access. The typography task samples used only task_tracker. Standard preset validation also ran. No account authorization or external Git/Slack action was exercised.",
    "Shared CSS is proven in actual scoped app/library output. Embedded browser behavior, Cloud/ACP and other conversation modes are source/compiler/unit coverage, not live claims.",
    "Skill, individual MCP and stacked template badges are live in all six themes at desktop/phone sizes; all 36 paired paint/geometry observations match. Native reordering/restoration persists across reload in Neutral/Paper at both viewport sizes. Phone is a narrow viewport with mouse dragging, not a native touch test.",
    "The +2px/-2px utilities and supports/fallback branches are compiler-equivalent. Existing unlayered shared card chrome suppresses reorder shadows in both builds; the film does not claim that edge painting was fixed. A separate keyless main diagnostic observes both actual target classes with computed box-shadow none during held native drags.",
    "Two owned unique unregistered-event automations were temporarily enabled for pinning/reordering, never dispatched, and disabled after capture. Both baseline and After run lists remain empty.",
    "The shared McpLogoBadge has a feature-map ownership gap; live scope was widened manually to MCP marketplace/template consumers. No feature map was edited."
